### ============================================


### Export / Import


### ============================================


### Export Budget Data

GET {{baseUrl}}/budget/export HTTP/1.1
X-User-ID: {{userId}}


### Import Budget Data

POST {{baseUrl}}/budget/import HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-ID: {{userId}}

{
  "expense_categories": [],
  "income_categories": [],
  "tags": [],
  "expenses": [],
  "incomes": [],
  "recurring_expense_rules": [],
  "recurring_income_rules": [],
  "expense_tags": [],
  "income_tags": []
}


### ============================================


### User Info


### ============================================


### Get Current User

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me HTTP/1.1
X-User-ID: {{userId}}


### ============================================


### Testing Notes


### ============================================

# How to use this file:
# 1. Login using the Login request to get a session_token cookie
# 2. Copy the session_token value from the response cookies
# 3. Update @userId at the top of this file with your user ID
# 4. Run any request - the X-User-ID header will be automatically set
#
# Endpoints implemented:
# - Expense Categories: full CRUD (soft delete via is_active)
# - Income Categories: full CRUD (soft delete via is_active)
# - Tags: full CRUD (hard delete)
# - Expenses: full CRUD + search + skip + check-skipped
# - Incomes: full CRUD + skip + check-skipped + occurrences
# - Priority Groups: hardcoded reference data
# - Budget Remaining: current month income - expenses
# - Stats: summary, trends, category-breakdown, savings-rate
# - Analysis: 50/30/20 breakdown by priority
# - Velocity: average monthly spending
# - Forecast: upcoming recurring expenses
# - Current Total Money: total income - total expenses
# - Month-over-Month: combined monthly trends
# - Recurring Expenses: read-only list of active rules
# - Recurring Incomes: full CRUD
# - Export/Import: JSON backup with ID remapping
